# Infrastructure Fix: Resolving Read-Only and Exited issues on ZimaOS

Our current goal is to stabilize the Coolify V4 infrastructure on ZimaOS to allow successful Git operations and Application deployments. 

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> To bypass ZimaOS's strict `Read-only` container root filesystem, we need to redirect the container's HOME directory and ensure full host-to-container permission mapping. This will require a restart of the Coolify V4 stack.

## Proposed Changes

### [Component] Coolify V4 Infrastructure (DeanOS)

#### [MODIFY] [docker-compose.yml](file:///DATA/AppData/coolify-v4/docker-compose.yml)
- **Environment:** Add `HOME=/var/www/html` to the `coolify-v4` service. This redirects SSH key generation from the restricted `/root/.ssh` to the writable app storage.
- **Volumes:** Ensure the `./ssh-root` mapping is robust.

#### [EXECUTE] [Server Commands]
1. **Permission Force:** Set `chmod -R 777 /DATA/AppData/coolify-v4/ssh-root` and `ssh` folders to eliminate any UID mismatches temporarily for diagnostics.
2. **Stack Restart:** `docker compose up -d --force-recreate`.

## Open Questions

> [!NOTE]
> - Hocam, şu an 'Exited' gören uygulama senin az önce ayağa kaldırmaya çalıştığımız yeni it-inventory mi? (Büyük ihtimalle evet). 
> - Bu değişiklikten sonra SSH anahtarını kaydetmeyi tekrar deneyeceğiz. 

## Verification Plan

### Automated Verification
- We will monitor the `coolify-v4` logs for any further `tee` or `permission denied` errors during Git/SSH operations.
- We will check if the `it-inventory` status turns GREEN (Healthy) in the Coolify UI.

### Manual Verification
- User to re-attempt the "Save Key" or "Deploy" action in the Coolify dashboard.
